# Katas

Gym for my grey matter when I'm bored and can't sleep.

## Build instructions

If you use VScode select the compiler with the CMake extension first. Then run the following to configure cmake.

```bash
$ mkdir build
$ cd build
$ cmake ..
```

A list of directories mirroring the ones in the root folder will be generated. Change directory into one of them and make their build target, for example:

```bash
$ cd build/SnailSort
$ make SnailSort -j 12 # To parallelize
```

Your brain will then start farting incontrollably, and there's nothing you can do about it.
Here's a picture of Heihaci Mishima to motivate you.

